docs/codex/10_analysis.log:677:**Implementation notes (2026-09-21, after codex gate 09, additive):** (i) C3F's `freezing` and C1P's `graph_partition` are passed as `torch.compile(options=...)` (with `triton.cudagraphs=True`, the reduce-overhead setting) rather than as global Inductor config changes, so that the compiled artifact's identity differs from the control arm built earlier in the same matched process (gate-09 finding 128); the arms' `compile_mode` records read `reduce-overhead+freezing` / `reduce-overhead+graph_partition`. (ii) E1's cast count is the ledger's X6a set (wrapper calls named `*_to_copy*` whose reads are all graph inputs), computed from the per-trace ideal-cost record and the compile dump (finding 129); E2's template count classifies extern GEMMs by the ideal-cost class and never counts SDPA kernels (finding 130). (iii) E4a's control is C3M only if C3M is also quality-eligible at both operating points (r1 VALID, validation PASS, SDR PASS, FULLY_GRAPHED); E1's lane stops when C3F's SDR gate fails (finding 131). (iv) The 5 % clock-drift rule is enforced by the audit between compared blocks (finding 132). (v) The C3 DC-filter operator's registered frame set gains 401 and 601 for the E9 held-out lengths, qualified on the pod only (finding 137). (vi) Any off-pod session-3 run is graded "engineering" by the audit (finding 136); A/A statistics are refreshed after the held-out A/A blocks (finding 138).
docs/codex/10_analysis.log:681:**Implementation note (2026-09-22, final shakedown, additive):** the session-3 clock sampler runs at 5 Hz (`CLOCK_LMS=200`) so that the 0.15 s timing blocks at 4,410 samples carry their own SM-clock samples for the registered 5 % drift rule; the audit scopes a drift violation to the affected restart (noted on the item) and fails a stage only when no clean eligible restart remains. Final shakedown (2026-09-22 02:04–05:53, 3.8 h, engineering grade): 189 of 191 mandatory items complete; the two remaining are the re-audit's tree identity (a later commit) and the C3 vs C3G pairs at 4,410 whose three restarts were all drift-flagged on the shared node (SM clock 6–7 % apart within the 1 Hz proxy window), an environmental condition of that host, not a harness defect.
