docs/codex/10_analysis.log:3030:   577	**E9 — Held-out crossover prediction (the anchor experiment; runs before E4a and E5).** Cost model `docs/phase3/probes/e9_cost_model.py` → `docs/phase3/e9/e9_cost_model.json` (sha256 recorded in `session3_config.json`), built ONLY from the 8 s and 100 ms trace decompositions (`docs/phase3/padbatch/decomposition_table.json`) and the four existing sweep points (headline walls at 4,410, 22,050, 88,200, 352,800). Terms of D(L) = wall(C3, L) − wall(H, L) (+ = H faster): fixed batching benefit B = 0.567 ms; non-GEMM front/tail and transformer-middle deltas linear in frames F = L/441 + 1; padded FLOPs 0.1609 GFLOP/frame at rate_H(F); kernel-efficiency term 0.4086 GFLOP/frame × (1/rate_H − 1/rate_C3) with saturating rate curves R·F/(F+h). Twelve variants were computed; the registered variant is the one with the smallest maximum in-sample residual, chosen before any held-out measurement: `sweep_refit_THNone_TCNone` (in-sample residuals at 4,410/22,050/88,200/352,800: +0.179, +0.140, -0.418, +0.093 ms; the 88,200 point is the hardest for every variant). **Registered predictions:** crossover L* = 261,072 samples (5.92 s); D(176,400) = +0.368 ms (H faster); D(264,600) = -0.015 ms (C3 faster by less than the model's own in-sample error, so the sign test at 6 s is weak and the magnitude test is the operative one; recorded as such). The traces-only variant (no sweep refit) gives L* = 219,177, D(176,400) = +0.188, D(264,600) = -0.200 and is recorded as the secondary reading. Already observed before this registration: 4,410, 22,050, 88,200 and 352,800; only 176,400 (4 s) and 264,600 (6 s) are held out, and those two lengths are never run on the shakedown host or in any ad-hoc process (`fullarms.held_out_guard`, `SESSION_POD=1` only inside the pod session). Measurement: eager-A validation references at both lengths, then matched C3 vs H, m1–m3, with the E6 A/A block (C3 vs C3, m1) at each length, protocol 5a. Pass (registered): predicted sign correct at both lengths and |observed − predicted| ≤ 0.4 ms at both (`e_tools.py e9_check`, observed = median over eligible restarts of the block medians, block-level bootstrap interval reported). Fail: report which term the residual points at (the per-term values are stored in the registration); do not refit and re-run.
docs/codex/10_analysis.log:3036:   583	**E5 — Structural-variation boundary test (optional; allowance 3,600 s).** Same model built through the pinned construction path (`get_model_from_config` on a derived yaml, `fullmodel/variants.py`) with depth ∈ {1, 6} × mask-estimator hidden width ∈ {full (mlp_expansion_factor 4), quarter (1)}, random weights (seed 20260921), timing only; validation = self-consistency against the variant's own eager-A reference (loose tier; no SDR claim). Arms C3 and H at both operating points, two restarts each (tags `v_<variant>_r1/r2`); node traces of C3 and H per variant at 4,410 (cast time, boundary count via graph verification, kernel sum and span via timing views); weight bytes per pass from parameter counts × 2 (`param_bytes_fp16` in every run record). The public architecture is depth 6 × full, so `d6_mfull` is the random-weight control for the headline arms. Predictions (registered): (i) C3's cast time and the boundary count are invariant to depth within 10 %; (ii) the 4,410 wall floor moves with mask-estimator weight bytes with slope ≈ bytes / 1.79 TB/s; (iii) transformer time scales linearly with depth. Kill: if the cast time scales with depth, the fixed-cost explanation is wrong; report it.
docs/codex/10_analysis.log:3042:   589	**Session plan (handoff §4).** Before the pod: every arm, wrapper and script above built and run end-to-end as a complete session on the shakedown host (GPU 4, tmux, `SHAKEDOWN=1`: E9 held-out cells recorded UNTESTED by rule and never run), on-node audit COMPLETE on that engineering data, one codex gate on the specs and the measurement path closed; the owner's go-ahead was given on 2026-09-21 for the measurement pod only ("only as instructed in the instructions"), and is requested again with the shakedown verdict attached before the pod is created. Order on the pod: E6 → E3 → E2 → E1 → E9 → E4a → E5 → E7. Stop and report, without retrying, if any planted fault passes, the SDR gate fails for a headline arm, clocks drift > 5 % between compared blocks, graph verification fails for an arm claimed graphed, a registered kill branch fires, or pod time exceeds 6 hours. Budget: `SESSION_BUDGET_S` 19,800 s (5.5 h) with a 900 s extraction reserve; target ≤ 3 GPU-h with E5/E7 as the registered cuts.
