docs/codex/10_analysis.log:3053:   600	**Implementation notes (2026-09-21, after codex gate 09, additive):** (i) C3F's `freezing` and C1P's `graph_partition` are passed as `torch.compile(options=...)` (with `triton.cudagraphs=True`, the reduce-overhead setting) rather than as global Inductor config changes, so that the compiled artifact's identity differs from the control arm built earlier in the same matched process (gate-09 finding 128); the arms' `compile_mode` records read `reduce-overhead+freezing` / `reduce-overhead+graph_partition`. (ii) E1's cast count is the ledger's X6a set (wrapper calls named `*_to_copy*` whose reads are all graph inputs), computed from the per-trace ideal-cost record and the compile dump (finding 129); E2's template count classifies extern GEMMs by the ideal-cost class and never counts SDPA kernels (finding 130). (iii) E4a's control is C3M only if C3M is also quality-eligible at both operating points (r1 VALID, validation PASS, SDR PASS, FULLY_GRAPHED); E1's lane stops when C3F's SDR gate fails (finding 131). (iv) The 5 % clock-drift rule is enforced by the audit between compared blocks (finding 132). (v) The C3 DC-filter operator's registered frame set gains 401 and 601 for the E9 held-out lengths, qualified on the pod only (finding 137). (vi) Any off-pod session-3 run is graded "engineering" by the audit (finding 136); A/A statistics are refreshed after the held-out A/A blocks (finding 138).
