codex
139. **BLOCKER — Published aggregates include restarts rejected by the clock rule.** [session3_result.py:48](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/fullmodel/session3_result.py:48), [ledger.py:609](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/fullmodel/ledger.py:609). Both use `pair_eligible` without applying the audit’s drift exclusions. At 4410, excluding affected restarts changes C3G **0.665033 → 0.687026 ms**, C3P **0.549410 → 0.574450 ms**, and X2a **−0.012523 → −0.024271 ms**; their intervals also change. **Minimal fix:** exclude the entire affected restart before computing medians, bootstrap intervals, walls, and ledger ratios.

140. **BLOCKER — COMPLETE 198/198 hides mandatory E6 clock failures.** [completeness.py:445](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/fullmodel/completeness.py:445), [completeness.py:451](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/fullmodel/completeness.py:451). E6 bypasses the clean-restart requirement: the sole 4410 A/A restart has **5.6% drift**, and every C3 and C1 headline restart at 4410 exceeds 5% within its blocks. Headline drift only becomes a note. Even under the final amendment’s relaxed rule, these comparisons have no clean restart. **Minimal fix:** enforce that rule for E6, mark the affected quantities UNRESOLVED, and propagate INCOMPLETE into the report.

141. **BLOCKER — “Extern GEMM” counts double-count templates.** [e_tools.py:117](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/fullmodel/e_tools.py:117). `ideal_costs.py` assigns Triton templates to class `GEMM`, so `ext` includes `tem`. The raw C3M traces contain **178 templates + 145 extern kernels** at 352800 and **280 + 30** at 4410; the report instead lists **323 and 310 extern kernels**. Extern timing totals likewise include template time. **Minimal fix:** exclude template rows from the extern subtotal while continuing to exclude SDPA.

142. **BLOCKER — E2’s gains receive an unsupported X6a attribution.** [session3_result.py:163](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/fullmodel/session3_result.py:163), [ledger.py:660](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/fullmodel/ledger.py:660). `_to_copy` in a template name is treated as proof that weight casts were fused. Both C3M traces still execute **420 parameter-only casts**, taking **0.905352/0.852058 ms**. The named templates consume fp16 weights already converted by preceding wrapper calls. Thus the reported E2 gains are incorrectly attributed partly to removing X6a casts. **Minimal fix:** remove that attribution unless the wrapper dataflow demonstrates the claimed removal.

143. **MAJOR — Analysis publishers bypass independent qualification and sample recomputation.** [session3_result.py:48](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/fullmodel/session3_result.py:48), [ledger.py:609](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/fullmodel/ledger.py:609), [e_tools.py:181](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/fullmodel/e_tools.py:181). CPU counterexample: changing only a cached matched median to **123 ms** makes the report and ledger return 123, although `qualify.pair_problems` rejects the record. **Minimal fix:** use a shared reducer that validates the payload and manifest, joins applicable quality and clock eligibility, and recomputes differences from samples.

144. **MAJOR — A/A pairing uses list position instead of repeat identity.** [e_tools.py:149](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/fullmodel/e_tools.py:149). Reordering the second arm’s block entries while retaining repeat IDs, timestamps, and samples passes the existing validator but changes the computed 8-s A/A median from **−0.090795 to −0.095193 ms**. **Minimal fix:** join blocks by unique repeat ID and compute their medians from samples before bootstrapping.

145. **MAJOR — Mandatory trace eligibility accepts absent or contradictory payloads.** [completeness.py:475](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/fullmodel/completeness.py:475), [completeness.py:482](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/fullmodel/completeness.py:482). CPU counterexamples leave all mandatory checks passing when every trace CSV is unreadable, or when `FULLY_GRAPHED` accompanies `qualified=False` and an empty `per_pass`. This permits mechanism numbers without qualifying evidence. **Minimal fix:** reuse the session-2 export-content checks and recompute graph qualification from all 50 passes.

146. **MAJOR — Intervention SDR eligibility trusts labels.** [completeness.py:489](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/fullmodel/completeness.py:489). Removing every C3M r1 SDR clip while retaining `status=PASS` leaves all session-3 mandatory checks passing, even though the shared validator returns an unresolved gate and the recomputed cell has SDR `NONE`. **Minimal fix:** validate the eight-clip payload and join its qualification to dependent pairs, preserving the registered quality-failure branches.

147. **MAJOR — E4a’s selected control and measured compile modes are not enforced.** [completeness.py:555](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/fullmodel/completeness.py:555), [completeness.py:562](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/fullmodel/completeness.py:562). CPU counterexamples pass when all valid E2 restarts show only **0.5 ms** improvement but E4a still selects C3M, or when matched C3N runs use `reduce-overhead` despite a `max-autotune` decision. Only the standalone r1 mode is compared. **Minimal fix:** rederive the decision from eligible E2 results and quality gates, then verify every matched and traced C3N mode.

148. **MAJOR — Missing count inputs become measured zeros.** [e_tools.py:101](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/fullmodel/e_tools.py:101), [e_tools.py:114](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/fullmodel/e_tools.py:114). A missing ideal-cost file produces zero template/extern counts; a selected cast whose timing row is missing silently contributes zero. These zeros also satisfy the audit’s finite-number checks. **Minimal fix:** require a qualified inventory and complete wrapper-to-row joins; emit UNRESOLVED for missing inputs. Reserve zero for a verified empty set.

149. **MAJOR — E9’s verdict mishandles ties and incomplete measurements.** [e_tools.py:193](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/fullmodel/e_tools.py:193), [e_tools.py:199](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/fullmodel/e_tools.py:199). CPU counterexamples produce **PASS** when the 264600 observation is exactly zero, incorrectly calling that “C3 faster,” and **FAIL** when one point passes but the other is missing. **Minimal fix:** require the registered strict sign at both points and both tolerance checks; return UNRESOLVED when a required observation is unavailable.

150. **MAJOR — Missing experiments generate substantive verdicts.** [session3_result.py:187](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/fullmodel/session3_result.py:187), [session3_result.py:286](/home/muhit/ms/sm120-nulltest/fullmodel/session3_result.py:286). With E1 pairs absent, the report says “within the ceiling.” With optional E7 evidence absent, it reports no overlap and withdraws the coefficient. Neither conclusion follows from missing evidence. **Minimal fix:** guard verdicts, ceiling comparisons, and withdrawal decisions with explicit input completeness; otherwise report UNRESOLVED.

ANALYSIS-READY: no

Raw sample checks reproduce E9 **+1.128826989/+0.672290684 ms**, E2 **+4.796455381/+0.198727590 ms**, and 8-s C3G/C3P **+1.403762493/+0.733635970 ms**. A/A medians reproduce **−0.050519593, −0.122959958, −0.090795103, −0.055970042 ms** at 176400, 264600, 352800, and 4410 respectively; the last lacks clock eligibility.

The X6a exceedance flag fires correctly at 8 s (**1.526×**). E5 arithmetic and units, figure CSV transformations, E9 model signs and single-term residual algebra reproduce their inputs. Actual E7 qualifying overlap exists, so its withdrawal condition does not fire.

Without `--phase3-dir`, all **38 Sep-20 ledger rows** remain identical to the pre-session-3 ledger.
